title: Authorizations › New case › Referral › Schedule intake
route: /authorizations/new/referral/RF-2053?draft=draft-1001
intro: After a referral is accepted, the full page books the intake visit and then marks the patient admitted. These two steps move a referral through Scheduled to Admitted.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Referral is Accepted\nFull page header"
click c1 "Click 'Schedule intake'"
overlay o1 "'Schedule intake'\n'RF-2053 · O.D., 33'"
input i1 "Pick a 'Date'\nStarts two days after the demo clock"
input i2 "Pick a 'Time'\nStarts at 9:00 am"
decision d1 "Is the date valid?"
process p1 "'Schedule intake' is disabled"
click c2 "Click 'Schedule intake'"
click cX "Click 'Cancel' or 'Close', press Escape,\nor click outside the dialog"
endx e1 "Nothing changes"
store st1 "Referral is Scheduled\nIntake time saved\nTimeline 'You scheduled the intake visit' and a dashed 'Intake visit' entry"
toast t1 "'Intake scheduled'\n'RF-2053 is Scheduled. Intake visit Thu 9:00 am.'"
screen sc1 "Header now shows 'Mark admitted' and 'Change intake'\nBanner 'Intake visit Thu 9:00 am'"
click c3 "Click 'Change intake'"
overlay o2 "'Change the intake visit'\nSame Date and Time, starting at the booked visit"
click c4 "Click 'Mark admitted'"
store st2 "Referral is Admitted\nTimeline 'Marked admitted'"
toast t2 "'Marked admitted'\n'RF-2053 counts as admitted in the funnel.'"
screen sc2 "Green banner 'Admitted into IOP'\nHeader has no decision buttons"
click c5 "Click 'Continue to medical records' on the banner\nor on the checklist"
goto g1 "Continues in: New case › Medical records › The checklist and Continue"

s1 --> c1 --> o1 --> i1 --> i2 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p1 --> cX
d1 -->|Yes| c2 --> st1 --> t1 --> sc1
o1 --> cX --> e1
sc1 --> c3 --> o2 --> c2
sc1 --> c4 --> st2 --> t2 --> sc2
sc1 --> c5 --> g1
